        <section id="what-is-defensive-programming?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>What is Defensive Programming?</h2>
              <p>Defensive programming is broad term which encompasses program design that ensures the continuing function of a piece of software under unforeseen circumstances so that it still behaves in a predictable manner despite unexpected actions.</p>
<p>Exception handling is one form of defensive programming. In our previous example, this dealt specifically with an error which caused a terminal error in the program. But what if we could anticipate a semantic error, where the program doesn’t but the functionality is not what was intended?</p>

          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
